+### The traffic light, 29 Oct 2026 (branch `feat/demo-polish`)
+
+A red, yellow or green light at the top of `/analysis`, `/advisory` and `/report`, drawn from `mvp_summary.band`, which is the 8th key of that dict. It was row 2 of the owner's feature table. After it the suite is 2,189 tests and the dictionaries 894 keys (7,152 values).
+
+- **The rule is the owner's own.** They confirmed it on 29 Oct 2026 ("It is my own rule"); nobody else has checked it. `build_mvp_summary` sets green when `status` is `good`, red when `priority` is `high` (not profitable, high repayment pressure or a household over its limit) and yellow otherwise. It reads the two verdicts that were already there, so it cannot disagree with the advice and adds no threshold and no model. Moderate risk, a funding gap and a plan not yet proven are yellow: each leaves something to check, not something wrong. Red wins over a yellow cause. `test_mvp_service.py` has a 12-case table, and the key-set tests (`test_household_income.py`, `test_mvp_api_contract.py`) and `test_log_privacy.py` were updated with it.
+- **The words are bounded.** Green says "no problem found in your figures", never "good to go" or "eligible", and the note under every light says it only reads the figures the person gave and is not a decision about a loan or a scheme. No eligibility rule is evaluated anywhere (`sc.eligUnchecked`), so a green light must not read as an approval. The note is on every light, not only the green one.
+- **Colour is never the only signal.** Green is a circle with a tick, yellow a triangle with an exclamation mark and red an octagon with a cross, each with the word beside it. Pale yellow is 1.37:1 against the light band, so every shape also has an outline in the text colour (13.8:1 in the light theme, 11.0:1 in the dark); a grayscale render of the print view keeps the triangle, its outline and the word. The `--band-glyph` token picks the glyph colour that reads on each fill in both themes.
+- **Where it sits.** On `/analysis` it replaces the old status mark; the old glyph-and-pill row is passed to `ResultBand` as children and drawn when the result carries no band, because a result stored before the light passes through `hydrate` untouched (drive's `old` pass covers it). On `/advisory` it is above the takeaway card. On `/report` it is its own item between the masthead and the main-result card, not part of either, because the feasibility card there is a different verdict and can disagree with the light.
+- **The strings.** `band.green`, `band.yellow`, `band.red` and `band.basis`, in all 8 languages. The 7 non-English sets are machine-written and no native speaker has read them; the Hindi ones go on the owner's review sheet (row 3).
+- **Print.** `.ui-band` is in the print `break-inside: avoid` list. `print-audit.mjs` keeps its own copy of that list and compares it with the stylesheet's on every run, and its first run after the change exited 2 because the copy lacked `.ui-band`. That is the check working, and the copy was updated; the run since exits 0 with 0 findings across 6 print renders.
+- **How it was checked.** The `drive` band check was written first and exited 1 with `BAND: 0 drawn` on all 19 loads of a result; on the finished component it exits 0 with 48 loads. Eight defects were planted, four in the component and four in the pages, and each failed `drive` on the loads meant for it (the list is in `tools/README.md`); the files were put back with `cp` and a `sha256` check. The `green` fixture (Sunita Patil, retail, Pune) was added because no other case reaches `good`.
+- **Trap: a backend started before the change.** It keeps serving the old Python, so the first `refresh-cases.mjs` wrote fixtures without a band and `drive` measured a page with nothing to draw. `refresh-cases.mjs` now exits 1 when a case's band differs from `EXPECTED_BAND` (`good` yellow, `nulls` and `empty` red, `green` green), and `drive` exits 2 for a fixture with no band. Restart the backend after any change to `services/`.
+- **The look, measured.** A one-off probe outside the repo took 48 renders of the light: each lamp on `/analysis` in the light and dark themes, at the largest text size, and at 320px in Malayalam and in Hindi at the smallest size; `/advisory` and `/report` at 1280px, and at 320px in Tamil and Bengali; the print view in grayscale; and 18 in-page renders in Hindi at 1280px and 360px. Each page had one light and none overflowed sideways. The label's contrast was at least 11.0:1, the note's 5.5:1, the outline's 11.0:1 and the glyph on its fill 6.4:1 (3:1 is the floor for graphics). The smallest sizes were 15.8px for the label and 13.2px for the note. Not changed: at 320px in Malayalam at the largest text the light is tall (the label takes up to 7 lines and the note 11) and one long word breaks at its edge, as it does in the other cards on the same page. Stacking the shape above the text at narrow widths would save about as much height as the shape adds in Hindi, so it was left.
+- **Gates run on the finished tree:** `drive`, `mobile-audit` (50 loads), `lang-layout` (112), `text-align`, `field-align` (96), `print-audit`, `figure-audit` (32 loads at 11 widths), `scroll-audit` (38 hops), `motion-audit`, `error-banner` (32 cases), `parity4`, `keycheck`, `glyph-audit`, ESLint and the whole backend suite, all with exit 0. The rest are run on the merged tree at the code freeze.
