rea, so the page holds it twice (the copy and the hidden original). The all-ten run gives 900 findings and not the 1,233 that the ten add up to, and the 333 were traced by comparing the ten single runs with the all-ten run kind by kind and by running some arms together in the scenario where they differ: WRONG-FIGURE 264 fewer (`banned`, `figure` and `leak` each give 132 on the same 132 checks and `default` gives 2 on one check, which is 398 on their own against 134 in the all-ten run), STRUCTURE 72 fewer (`default` 58 and `overflow` 104 against 90), FIGURE-WRAP 4 fewer, and LIVE-REGION 5 more, BANNED-WORD 1 more and LEAK 1 more, so 264 + 72 + 4 − 5 − 1 − 1 = 333. Why one arm changes what another finds was not examined, apart from the 132 checks that three arms share. The scripts that made the comparison are not in the repo.
