+**320px, and the results label, 29 Oct 2026 (branch `feat/demo-polish`).** The audit's narrowest width had been 360. A one-off probe at 320 found that on `/advisory` the label "Step 3 of 4 · Your results" stuck out of its row by 28.9px in Malayalam at the largest text, and the page scrolled sideways by 17px (`scrollWidth` 337 against 320). The cause was in the row, not the label: `.ui-progress-label` was `flex: 0 0 auto` in a `nowrap` flex row, and the four bars were `flex: 1` with no floor, so a long label took what it needed and the bars got 3px, then 0 (`dots` read 0/0/0/0). The progress strip therefore showed no progress at all, which is worse than the overflow. Fix, in `index.css`: the row wraps, each bar has a `1.5rem` basis (`flex: 1 0 1.5rem`) and the label may shrink (`flex: 0 1 auto; min-width: 0`). When the label would squeeze a bar under 1.5rem it drops beneath four full-width bars; otherwise nothing changes (at the normal text size, Tamil at 360 and English at 320 still show the label beside the bars).
+
+Red then green, same probe over 96 loads (2 widths × 8 languages × 3 text sizes × 2 routes): before, 1 overhang; after, 0, with the bars at least about 23px wide or full width. `mobile-audit` gained a `320-stress` viewport (Malayalam, dark, largest text) and a per-viewport `routes` list. With the fix reverted it exits 1 (`320-stress_advisory` and `320-stress_report`, OVERFLOW +17px and 4 CLIP each); with it applied it exits 0 over 50 loads. **The viewport runs two routes on purpose.** The first full run at 320 failed in 7 loads for reasons that predate this fix and are not the label: a word wider than its box in the landing page's heading (+17px sideways), the category buttons on `/business`, the customers disclosure on `/location`, the section title and consent line on `/finance`, and the scheme-fit chart's labels on `/analysis` and `/schemes`. A gate that fails for good gets ignored, so those stay **open** and the `routes` list is widened as each is fixed. Nobody has read the Malayalam strings for sense; the probe measures boxes only.
